1
00:00:02,150 --> 00:00:06,450
There are strange phenomenon
in this world

2
00:00:06,450 --> 00:00:09,700
that science is unable to explain.

3
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:12,590
When people came
face to face with them,

4
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:17,220
all they can do is tremble
upon the terror of the darkness.

5
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:22,490
But there are those who fight every day
to shine a ray of hope

6
00:00:22,490 --> 00:00:25,350
into that chaotic darkness.

7
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:27,710
People call them...

8
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:30,600
Yokai Hunter.

9
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,560
This is the city, huh?

10
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:40,320
The city with the "Divine Tree"
that was the talk of variety shows.

11
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:42,250
Now then...

12
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:46,560
Which one will it be?
Demons or serpents?

13
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:52,150
(MOB MOB WOW!)

14
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:55,030
(MOB MOB WOW!)

15
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,870
(MOB MOB WOW!)

16
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:00,700
(MOB MOB WOW!)

17
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:04,830
I realized that our youth is Grey

18
00:01:04,830 --> 00:01:07,750
The origin of this uneasiness
Is yet unknown

19
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:10,250
Trains of emotions keep running
Through my brain

20
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:13,420
Struggling through this adolescence

21
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:16,380
Don't disturb my deep psyche

22
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:19,050
Who is that behind you?

23
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:22,850
Opposing ideas creates distortion

24
00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:26,270
Exorcise all the sorrow

25
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:29,940
So, do what you can now

26
00:01:30,020 --> 00:01:31,860
My life

27
00:01:32,110 --> 00:01:35,990
Finally, break it down

28
00:01:37,490 --> 00:01:40,320
(Want) Both greed
(Young) And honesty

29
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:43,200
(Burn) Are growing
(1) On this chest of mine

30
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,960
(Trance) I'm not waking up
(Chance) I want to wake up

31
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:48,920
(Stance) These two different faces of mine
(1) Are standing back-to-back

32
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:51,420
Taking things as it is

33
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:54,840
In this free relation where
We resent each other

34
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:57,130
Once these two become one

35
00:01:57,130 --> 00:01:59,140
That smile becomes one

36
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:02,220
And only "1"(MOB MOB WOW!)

37
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:05,890
"1"(MOB MOB WOW!)

38
00:02:06,230 --> 00:02:07,310
(MOB MOB WOW!)

39
00:02:07,310 --> 00:02:10,190
One and only "1"(MOB MOB WOW!)

40
00:02:10,350 --> 00:02:11,900
"1"

41
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,070
(MOB MOB WOW!)

42
00:02:13,070 --> 00:02:15,360
One and only "1"

43
00:02:16,990 --> 00:02:21,490
(Yokai Hunter Haruaki Amakusa appears!
~The Threat of Hyakki! ~)

44
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:25,710
Are there still anyone
who isn't assigned to a duty?

45
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:27,880
Okay, if you don't have
anything in mind,

46
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:31,500
then Niido, Sagure, Kageyama,
and Inukawa,

47
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:33,520
you're in charge of costumes.

48
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,580
This is the worst!

49
00:02:35,770 --> 00:02:38,840
Costumes are the most important
part of a haunted house,

50
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:40,840
so please do your best.

51
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:43,800
Wouldn't sheets be enough?

52
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:45,880
Just wear a white sheet,

53
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:48,480
and say, "I'm a ghost~".
That's good enough, right?

54
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:52,400
Oh, then we don't have
to bother making anything!

55
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:57,020
Niido, you really are...

56
00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:00,490
A freaking genius, man!

57
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:05,180
That's great, right, Mob?
We don't have to be stuck in sewing hell.

58
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:08,180
Is that really okay?

59
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:12,120
You're just giving a white cloth
to the ones portraying the ghosts.

60
00:03:12,370 --> 00:03:16,710
As the ones responsible for the costumes,
shouldn't we try a bit harder?

61
00:03:16,830 --> 00:03:18,640
Oh come on, Kageyama.

62
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:23,180
So can you make something?
Do you even have any good ideas?

63
00:03:23,770 --> 00:03:26,510
If you have anything to say,
then say it.

64
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:32,470
Flapflapflapflapflap.

65
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:34,560
Do you get what he's saying?

66
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:37,570
(Progress until Mob explodes: 22%)

67
00:03:37,570 --> 00:03:39,070
(Student Council Room)

68
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:44,010
Those that want to serve food
at the festival have to take a stool test,

69
00:03:44,010 --> 00:03:46,490
please inform
all the class representatives.

70
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:47,760
President.

71
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,250
Hmm? What is it, Kageyama?

72
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:54,760
I think the themes are getting
a bit too extreme this year.

73
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:59,450
This concert plan is bound to cause noise
complaints from neighboring houses.

74
00:03:59,550 --> 00:04:00,800
Not only that...

75
00:04:00,910 --> 00:04:03,240
There's also the cross-dressing cafe!
It's just absurd!

76
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:06,810
It might be a cultural festival, but we
should keep our looks in moderation!

77
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:10,750
I think they're fine as long as
they keep the safety precautions.

78
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:11,640
What?!

79
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,440
I agree,

80
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:17,040
but just in case,
we'll give them another reminder.

81
00:04:17,230 --> 00:04:19,190
Would that be satisfactory?

82
00:04:20,670 --> 00:04:22,070
Yes...

83
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:26,410
Then time flies by.

84
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:30,330
The Culture Festival is now
two weeks away.

85
00:04:30,790 --> 00:04:33,760
They're making steady progress...

86
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:37,240
If we do nothing, it'll be really bad.

87
00:04:38,170 --> 00:04:39,980
This is bad...

88
00:04:40,230 --> 00:04:42,380
Gotta think of a way
to raise the numbers...

89
00:04:42,890 --> 00:04:44,640
The site traffic is low.

90
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:46,190
Thank you for waiting.

91
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:47,730
Oh, thanks.

92
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:50,320
So, what is it that
you want to talk about?

93
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,060
Actually...

94
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:54,040
(Night Middle School)

95
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,630
I see.

96
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:57,910
So you want to commute here?

97
00:04:57,910 --> 00:04:59,740
This is pretty sudden.

98
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:02,930
I'm thinking of retaking
compulsory education.

99
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:08,200
It's a night school, so I will need
to finish my shift by 4 PM, so...

100
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,490
He's trying to improve himself, huh?

101
00:05:10,670 --> 00:05:12,340
That's fine.

102
00:05:12,450 --> 00:05:15,580
-Go at it.
-T-thank you very much!

103
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:19,590
Well, Mob's still here.
We'll probably be fine.

104
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:23,100
As for Dimple, I barely see him lately.

105
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:26,400
Probably should've put a collar on him.

106
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:31,160
Excuse me!

107
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:35,010
My name is Haruaki Amakusa,
a Yokai Hunter!

108
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:36,150
Mama, that guy...

109
00:05:36,150 --> 00:05:38,770
Is what I'll say when I enter.

110
00:05:39,330 --> 00:05:42,500
Excuse me. My name is...

111
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:44,640
Excuse mee...

112
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,120
Eexcusee me!

113
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:48,000
My name is Haruaki...

114
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,100
All right!

115
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:50,770
Exsqueeze me!

116
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:55,280
E-excuse me!

117
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:58,540
I'm Haruaki Amakusa!

118
00:05:59,290 --> 00:06:01,500
What is your business here?

119
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,200
I am the one who hunts "Them".

120
00:06:04,350 --> 00:06:06,820
Let's see, for now,
let's just call them...

121
00:06:07,530 --> 00:06:11,530
They are "Those that dwell in the darkness",
and I am their hunter.

122
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:17,270
I came to this city to prevent
"That incident" from happening again.

123
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:21,090
I can barely understand
what he's saying.

124
00:06:21,450 --> 00:06:25,630
I'm sorry, but we have a client
coming that needs exorcising.

125
00:06:25,750 --> 00:06:28,500
Can you please wait outside?

126
00:06:32,090 --> 00:06:36,370
I probably have no right to say this,
but that's one weird customer.

127
00:06:38,710 --> 00:06:40,390
He's being questioned.

128
00:06:40,590 --> 00:06:42,910
He's going to get taken
to the police station.

129
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:48,560
Thank you so very much,
Master Reigen.

130
00:06:49,950 --> 00:06:51,290
Phew.

131
00:06:51,370 --> 00:06:54,320
-Let's take a break, shall we?
-Oh, okay.

132
00:06:55,910 --> 00:06:57,850
Are you free now?

133
00:06:58,340 --> 00:07:00,630
It is I, Haruaki Amakusa.

134
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:03,310
He didn't get taken away...

135
00:07:04,250 --> 00:07:09,360
Now then, about the "Dark Troops"...

136
00:07:09,550 --> 00:07:12,410
I thought it was
"Those that dwell in the darkness".

137
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:17,100
"They" have more than one name.

138
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:20,290
Also, I suggest you don't say
those names easily.

139
00:07:20,430 --> 00:07:22,250
You might get "Killed".

140
00:07:22,410 --> 00:07:26,040
The "Vortex of Madness"
is most definitely spreading.

141
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:31,720
I would like to ask for your cooperation,
so we can sever the "Chain of Sadness".

142
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:35,680
Umm, dear customer,
I'm afraid I don't follow...

143
00:07:35,790 --> 00:07:38,680
-I am not a customer.
-Huh?

144
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:44,540
I am the hunter of the darkness...
in the dark... uh...

145
00:07:46,210 --> 00:07:49,800
"The hunter of those
that lurk within darkness."

146
00:07:50,030 --> 00:07:53,280
Haruaki Amakusa, a Yokai Hunter.

147
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,740
Shut up!

148
00:07:54,740 --> 00:08:00,000
I'm fed up listening to all
the pretentious words you're spitting out!

149
00:08:00,170 --> 00:08:01,960
T-that's not what I'm...

150
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:06,310
Don't get carried away and purposely
pick hard to understand words, you idiot!

151
00:08:06,310 --> 00:08:09,270
I don't have time to listen
to your nonsense!

152
00:08:09,270 --> 00:08:14,060
Get to the point or get out! Otherwise,
I'll pluck that lock of hair of yours!

153
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:16,260
O-okay...

154
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:27,120
There are yokais threatening
peace in the world of men.

155
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:37,010
I, Haruaki Amakusa, am a Yokai Hunter,
therefore I hunt Yokai for a living.

156
00:08:37,130 --> 00:08:41,690
For the traces of Yokai led me
to this Seasoning City, and thus...

157
00:08:41,690 --> 00:08:43,270
A-ahem!

158
00:08:43,270 --> 00:08:46,800
I'm going after the evil
Yokai group, Hyakki.

159
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:49,790
Their goal is to resurrect
the Great Yokai King,

160
00:08:49,790 --> 00:08:55,090
and are preparing to drain a huge amount
of energy to achieve that goal.

161
00:08:56,970 --> 00:08:59,850
His way of speaking went
back to normal midway.

162
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:02,350
Must be hard to talk like that.

163
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:05,740
The ominous aura grows day by day.

164
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:08,070
Honestly, I am worried.

165
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:10,520
How about you ask the police?

166
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:12,430
The police are not an option.

167
00:09:12,430 --> 00:09:14,490
"They" would immediately...

168
00:09:14,670 --> 00:09:21,200
...pull a "Violation of Swords and Firearms
Possession Control Law" and arrest me!

169
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,600
Of course they would.

170
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,740
A-anyway, I need your help
against the Hyakki...

171
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:26,390
Cut the bullcrap already!

172
00:09:26,510 --> 00:09:29,150
I've had enough of playing
around with you.

173
00:09:29,150 --> 00:09:31,140
We're running a business here, okay?

174
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:33,470
-Leave already, will you?
-You mean...

175
00:09:33,470 --> 00:09:36,580
You will help as long as I pay
the consultation fee?

176
00:09:39,690 --> 00:09:42,200
Would a million yen be enough?

177
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:47,850
You think this stack of notebook
papers would fool me?

178
00:09:49,670 --> 00:09:50,480
Huh?

179
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,120
It's... It's real?!

180
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:59,090
My parents are rich,
and they support my activities.

181
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:01,910
-All right. Let's go, Serizawa.
-Huh?

182
00:10:02,050 --> 00:10:03,870
We shall exterminate the "Hyakki!"

183
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:09,020
If the "Great Yokai King" is resurrected,
then the world would fall into "Darkness!"

184
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:11,460
We will erase the "Vortex of Madness,"

185
00:10:12,810 --> 00:10:15,440
and sever the "Chain of Sadness!"

186
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,800
Y-yes, Sir!

187
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:21,320
I finally made friends.
Such happiness.

188
00:10:21,690 --> 00:10:24,270
A Yokai Hunter is always alone
on their duty.

189
00:10:24,270 --> 00:10:27,020
They always fight alone.

190
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:30,830
It has been so long
since I've felt human warmth.

191
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:32,660
I thank you.

192
00:10:34,510 --> 00:10:36,650
Hey, Mob. What's wrong?

193
00:10:36,730 --> 00:10:39,780
Oh, sorry. There's something
I want to discuss with you.

194
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:43,600
Oh, I'll listen after we finish this case.

195
00:10:43,770 --> 00:10:45,390
Come with us.

196
00:10:45,390 --> 00:10:46,880
What are we doing?

197
00:10:46,990 --> 00:10:49,130
It's a Yokai extermination.

198
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,110
We're severing the Chain of Sadness.

199
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:54,410
Okay...?

200
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:56,450
Forgive me, young boy.

201
00:10:56,550 --> 00:10:58,880
This is an "Emergency."

202
00:10:59,010 --> 00:11:01,620
Women and children
shouldn't come with us.

203
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:05,220
Nah, it'll be fine for Mob.

204
00:11:13,830 --> 00:11:15,910
Seems like this isn't the place, either.

205
00:11:15,910 --> 00:11:20,120
Don't tell me he's actually
just a cosplayer.

206
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,940
Oh well, as long as he pays
the consultation fee.

207
00:11:24,570 --> 00:11:25,720
Over there!

208
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:28,420
There's a slight Yokai presence
from there!

209
00:11:28,590 --> 00:11:31,890
It's the place where we performed
an exorcism back then.

210
00:11:31,890 --> 00:11:35,450
You completely vaporized
the evil spirit, right?

211
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:37,420
Only two weeks left...

212
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:42,410
I do feel some weird energy out of there.

213
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:43,770
Is that so?

214
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:45,880
Let's go, then.

215
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:49,890
Speaking of which, how much budget
do we have for the costumes, anyway?

216
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:56,870
This is absolutely the place.
No mistaking it.

217
00:11:56,970 --> 00:11:59,480
(Progress until Mob explodes: 31%)

218
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:10,310
The space itself is warped.

219
00:12:10,310 --> 00:12:12,670
It's the yokais doing, no doubt.

220
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:14,570
Curse you, Hyakki.

221
00:12:14,570 --> 00:12:17,450
It appears they plan on turning
this place into their stronghold.

222
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:19,690
So the yokais are real?

223
00:12:19,870 --> 00:12:23,760
So he's not just some
random cosplayer.

224
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,500
Plant roots?

225
00:12:37,530 --> 00:12:40,740
What's wrong, Amakusa?
You're sweating a lot.

226
00:12:42,380 --> 00:12:43,900
The truth is...

227
00:12:44,010 --> 00:12:48,930
My experience in fighting yokais
is limited to one-on-one fights.

228
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:51,840
Even then, I always only
barely made it out alive.

229
00:12:51,950 --> 00:12:56,280
Against a single opponent,
with full preparations on my side,

230
00:12:56,280 --> 00:13:00,750
I only managed to exterminate it
after three days and nights.

231
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:02,470
But this time,

232
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:07,760
we're right inside the evil Yokai group
Hyakki's headquarters, it's way beyond...

233
00:13:08,010 --> 00:13:09,130
What's wrong?!

234
00:13:09,130 --> 00:13:12,690
This wall is pretty sticky, man.

235
00:13:13,170 --> 00:13:16,140
We can use jelly to scare customers!

236
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,170
What now?!

237
00:13:18,170 --> 00:13:20,400
Our way back!

238
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:21,990
It's sealed up.

239
00:13:22,110 --> 00:13:25,860
I guess our only choice is to take out
the one warping the space itself.

240
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:28,120
You're pretty calm, Serizawa.

241
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:31,730
Oh, dark and closed spaces
calm me down.

242
00:13:31,730 --> 00:13:34,080
We'll make it using cardboard
and duct tape,

243
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:35,930
then we'll have to measure
the height of the ghost actor...

244
00:13:35,930 --> 00:13:38,590
Anyway, our only choice is forward.

245
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:41,620
Just accept your fate, Yokai Hunter.

246
00:13:42,850 --> 00:13:45,570
My stomach is killing me...

247
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:58,060
Reigen, behind you!

248
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:02,320
There you are, Yokai!

249
00:14:03,550 --> 00:14:08,050
O' spirit of something, something,
and something!

250
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:11,620
Grant me strength!

251
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:17,620
Holy Sword!
Kusanagi no Daihannya Kagemitsu!

252
00:14:21,770 --> 00:14:24,300
My holy sword!

253
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:34,760
Oh, so the normal exorcism
method works.

254
00:14:35,250 --> 00:14:37,630
What manner of power is that...?

255
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,540
They're all coming out
one after another.

256
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:41,820
They're coming in all directions!

257
00:14:41,820 --> 00:14:45,450
We're in deep trouble.
I can't even think.

258
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:48,110
I'll weaken them by throwing salts.

259
00:14:48,110 --> 00:14:50,900
I leave the rest to you,
Mob and Serizawa!

260
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,030
Yes, Sir!

261
00:14:52,650 --> 00:14:54,300
Take this!

262
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:56,610
Salt Splash!

263
00:14:56,720 --> 00:15:00,870
Oh, salt throwing could be
a good attraction.

264
00:15:03,970 --> 00:15:05,420
I see.

265
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:08,880
If we put a ghost than can be exorcised,
then maybe even kids will find it fun.

266
00:15:20,090 --> 00:15:21,980
T-that's...

267
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:25,650
The Four Hell Lords of Hyakki?!

268
00:15:25,870 --> 00:15:28,810
And not to mention, behind them is...

269
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:31,570
...the Great Yokai King!

270
00:15:31,790 --> 00:15:34,990
He's already resurrected!

271
00:15:35,420 --> 00:15:37,450
Lowly humans.

272
00:15:37,590 --> 00:15:40,910
They are the Four Hell Lords of Hyakki.

273
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:45,550
You shall be cast into
the abyss of terror.

274
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:47,590
It's over...

275
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:49,790
I'm so sorry I dragged you to this.

276
00:15:50,510 --> 00:15:53,280
If this is that bad,
should we run away?

277
00:15:53,350 --> 00:15:54,970
I don't think that's possible.

278
00:15:54,970 --> 00:15:58,890
Yes, I don't think my design sense
is good enough to make one.

279
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:33,510
They took down two in an instant?!

280
00:16:33,610 --> 00:16:36,060
Just who are they?

281
00:16:36,530 --> 00:16:38,310
They are psychics.

282
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:43,290
How could such omnipotent powers
exist in this world?

283
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:45,660
H-how enviable.

284
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:52,720
Yeah, of course you'd thought that way.

285
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:55,200
But to them,
those powers aren't that useful.

286
00:16:59,710 --> 00:17:04,250
You didn't just defeat members of Hyakki,
but even the Four Hell Lords.

287
00:17:04,250 --> 00:17:06,870
Not bad, lowly humans.

288
00:17:07,450 --> 00:17:09,710
However!

289
00:17:14,090 --> 00:17:19,720
Don't think you can win against
the Great Yokai King!

290
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:24,480
W-what incredible powers...

291
00:17:24,670 --> 00:17:28,010
Would you two be interested
in becoming Yokai Hunters?

292
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:30,860
Of course, I will be sure to give you
plenty of monthly salaries!

293
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:33,200
What?! H-hey, you two...!

294
00:17:33,290 --> 00:17:36,240
I don't think I can do it.
I still want to study.

295
00:17:36,330 --> 00:17:40,550
Sorry, I'm fully focused
on the cultural festival for now.

296
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:42,760
Cultural festival...?

297
00:17:43,030 --> 00:17:44,810
Too bad for you, huh?

298
00:17:44,810 --> 00:17:48,120
They're already full
from their daily life.

299
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:52,740
Amakusa, if you think you can make
everyone bend with stacks of money,

300
00:17:52,950 --> 00:17:55,010
then you're sorely mistaken!

301
00:17:56,250 --> 00:17:57,950
Forgive me, Reigen!

302
00:17:57,950 --> 00:18:02,010
You believed my story
as a friend, and yet!

303
00:18:02,010 --> 00:18:05,410
I tried to buy your cooperation
using money!

304
00:18:05,410 --> 00:18:07,920
Please forgive my shameful conduct!

305
00:18:08,010 --> 00:18:09,450
Wait, no!

306
00:18:09,450 --> 00:18:13,050
I'm personally okay
with the consultation fee... ack!

307
00:18:13,970 --> 00:18:15,080
Ahem...

308
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:17,090
Y-yes, I see.

309
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:18,940
As long as you understand.

310
00:18:19,050 --> 00:18:22,620
Reigen, I am truly grateful.

311
00:18:23,630 --> 00:18:27,150
Now that I look at it,
that's quite the striking design.

312
00:18:27,270 --> 00:18:30,800
Maybe we can make a stuffing out of it
and sell it for profit?

313
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:34,520
They're an apparition, so...

314
00:18:34,810 --> 00:18:37,200
He'll turn to dust soon, too.

315
00:18:37,290 --> 00:18:38,860
I see...

316
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:41,860
That's it!

317
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:44,750
So,

318
00:18:44,990 --> 00:18:47,710
he's actually a real Yokai Hunter.

319
00:18:47,910 --> 00:18:50,440
Some jobs are really out there, huh?

320
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:52,700
Let's have ramen and go home.

321
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:55,570
Oh, I have something I have to do, so...

322
00:18:55,570 --> 00:18:59,100
Oh? So what was that thing
you want to discuss again?

323
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:02,240
It's okay, I found a solution.

324
00:19:02,570 --> 00:19:04,250
I'll be going.

325
00:19:06,090 --> 00:19:09,970
Mob solved a problem by himself...

326
00:19:12,510 --> 00:19:16,400
Inukawa, I got an idea
about the costume.

327
00:19:16,570 --> 00:19:19,360
Can you come to the classroom
early tomorrow?

328
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:23,310
What?! I thought we decided
on the white sheets!

329
00:19:23,490 --> 00:19:26,440
No, I think we should try our best.

330
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:29,900
Everyone is working hard
on their duty, after all.

331
00:19:57,870 --> 00:20:01,840
And so, the day of
the cultural festival arrives.

332
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:10,930
The reaction to the costume Mob
and Inukawa made were rather mediocre,

333
00:20:11,070 --> 00:20:14,110
but there were no complaints.

334
00:20:16,450 --> 00:20:20,070
As for the reaction from
the customers...

335
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:22,460
I see.

336
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:25,530
It's pretty well made
for middle schooler level.

337
00:20:33,390 --> 00:20:36,440
That's quite the striking design...

338
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:41,940
-I'm glad we did it.
-Yeah, I guess.

339
00:20:42,110 --> 00:20:44,160
That was pretty tiring, though.

340
00:20:44,310 --> 00:20:47,220
Yeah, I'm glad we did it.

341
00:20:48,010 --> 00:20:49,460
(Today's Maids)

342
00:20:49,550 --> 00:20:51,180
Thank you for waiting.

343
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:55,030
Here's your Forest Bear
Lickety-Lick Soda,

344
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:58,030
and your Dreaming Hoppity
Hop Bunny Cola.

345
00:20:58,030 --> 00:21:00,300
Oh my, so cute!

346
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:02,830
All the boys are wearing maid outfits!

347
00:21:02,830 --> 00:21:04,990
Let me take a picture!

348
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:07,040
Enjoy your stay...

349
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:09,730
We have another customer!

350
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:11,970
Hey there, Ritsu...

351
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:15,920
That's one heck of an outfit
you have there...

352
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:18,750
Well, it kinda fits you, though.

353
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:27,050
(Spirits and Such Consultation Office)

354
00:21:30,470 --> 00:21:32,520
All right, that should do it.

355
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,070
This should increase traffic.

356
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:44,320
The blue light shined
Dazzling my eye at 01:30 AM

357
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:49,700
Even as I swiped the page over,
The smiles of friends besides me remain

358
00:21:59,710 --> 00:22:02,130
Yes, I want someone to understand

359
00:22:02,130 --> 00:22:04,630
All the colorless and transparent wishes

360
00:22:04,630 --> 00:22:07,130
All the breath stuck within
The depth of my heart

361
00:22:07,130 --> 00:22:09,760
Suddenly flowed out
Bringing my consciousness back

362
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:12,220
I remember the days hung dry

363
00:22:12,220 --> 00:22:14,720
The very normal days passed by

364
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:17,190
Even if reality is corrupted

365
00:22:17,190 --> 00:22:19,940
The sky we saw together
Was definitely real

366
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:24,650
It's harder to understand than
The grammar on the blackboard

367
00:22:24,650 --> 00:22:29,860
The story that disappears
Under 24 hours makes me sad and lonely

368
00:22:30,130 --> 00:22:34,330
It's so hard, and I find myself
On the verge of giving up again and again

369
00:22:34,330 --> 00:22:35,870
But I...

370
00:22:36,700 --> 00:22:40,040
The current me will no longer give up

371
00:22:40,170 --> 00:22:45,050
Overflowing emotions on my sleeve,
Running through worry and doubt

372
00:22:45,050 --> 00:22:50,260
Nobody has decided if the future is 0 or 100,
So I'll paint over them myself

373
00:22:50,260 --> 00:22:55,680
Even if my existence itself can't be proven,
If this world struck me in my heart

374
00:22:55,810 --> 00:22:58,350
I will flood it with cobalt blue

375
00:23:26,270 --> 00:23:28,350
What? Mob is starting to get popular?

376
00:23:28,350 --> 00:23:31,220
He got super popular among women,
and was even elected as a founder?

377
00:23:31,220 --> 00:23:32,850
All right, go at it, Mob!

378
00:23:32,970 --> 00:23:35,140
Next on episode three of
Mob Psycho 100 III,

379
00:23:35,250 --> 00:23:37,030
"Conceited ~100%~"

380
00:23:37,210 --> 00:23:39,820
Recording it?
That's also a wise decision.
